design/bom.csv:62:Charging pads x4,"CP1,CP2,CP3,CP4",4,"charging pads on the INSIDE face of the band at the point opposite the block (180 degrees), in a row around the band, in the resin liner and not in the metal body, gold-plated flush with the liner, order VBUS, D-, D+, GND (architecture 17.12)",,,round pad,1.6 dia,gold pad 1.6 mm,"4 pads, 2.4 mm pitch along the arc, 0.07 mm thick, set in the liner; the row stands at X = -1.0 mm from the band's middle (architecture 17.15 and 17.28; design/mfg/specs/band-flex-tails.md and band-liner.md); wired in flex tail B (other side); the pebble case (17.12) mates with them",CALC,"design/architecture.md section 17.1, 17.3",,"Design partner (ring maker) must answer: pad part or plating, how the pads are set in the resin liner and wired to the tail, and the mating contact of the case"
design/mfg/assembly/assembly.md:144:- **Join:** CP1 (`pad_VBUS`), CP2 (`pad_D-`), CP3 (`pad_D+`), CP4 (`pad_GND`) to the four pad lands of FLEX2 (`band_flex_away`). How the pad is made is open (`design/bom.csv:61`: "pad part or plating"). [PROPOSED default: the land itself is the pad, with thick hard gold; reason, a soldered disc adds a joint that sweat reaches through the liner edge.] The disc of the model is 1.6 mm, 0.07 thick, flush with the liner's inner face (`design/mech/thin/placement.csv:43`).
